# .gitattributes
#
# WHAT   Line-ending and binary rules for Git.
# FOR    Keeping files identical on every operating system: without this, a checkout on Windows can turn every
#        file into CRLF, which shows up as whole-file diffs and confuses tools. Source is always LF; images and
#        fonts are never touched.
# DEBUG  - Every line of a file shows as changed: your editor or Git config converted line endings; this file
#          forces LF on checkout, so run `git add --renormalize .` once. `npm run check:portable` lists any CRLF
#          file that slipped in.
#
# Author: Giordano Bertin-Maurice
# Copyright (c) 2026 Giordano Bertin-Maurice. All rights reserved.

# Keep line endings identical on every operating system. Without this, a checkout on Windows
# can turn every file into CRLF, which shows up as whole-file diffs and confuses tools.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch their bytes
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
